  "name": "Generate LinkedIn posts with Nano Banana AI images and auto post them from Google Sheets",
  "tags": [],
  "nodes": [
    {
      "id": "73de490d-4741-463b-a539-7a18938f3af0",
      "name": "Sticky Note",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -643,
        -97
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "width": 520,
        "height": 771,
        "content": "## Write LinkedIn posts with an AI image and post them from a list of topics\nTurn topics from Google Sheets into LinkedIn posts with their own image: every weekday Gemini writes the post, Nano Banana draws the image and PostWire publishes both on LinkedIn, Facebook and Bluesky.\n\n### How it works\n1. **Every weekday at 9:00** reads the rows marked ready. **Take the next topic** picks the first and **Mark the topic as writing** claims it.\n2. **Write the posts with Gemini** returns a LinkedIn post, a shorter Facebook and Bluesky version and the brief for the image.\n3. **Nano Banana image** (Gemini) generates the image from that brief.\n4. **Post to LinkedIn, Facebook, Bluesky** (PostWire) uploads the image and publishes each text on its network.\n5. **Mark the topic as posted** writes the post links in the row. When the image or a network fails, **Write the fix in the row** and **Email me the fix** tell you what to fix.\n\n### Setup\n1. Install the verified **PostWire** node (search \"PostWire\" in the nodes panel), create an account at postwire.io, connect your networks and paste your API key into a **PostWire API** credential.\n2. Add a Google Gemini credential to both Gemini nodes. The text fits the free tier; a Nano Banana image costs about 0.04 USD.\n3. Create a sheet with the columns topic, notes, status, posted_at, links and note. Write ready in status to queue a topic, and pick the sheet in the four Sheets nodes.\n4. Connect Gmail and fill in **Post settings**.\n\n### Customize\nChange the voice and image style in Post settings, or the networks in the PostWire node (the free plan posts to 2 networks per post)."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
